\operatorname{arccos}⁡x$ for $x\\in [0,1].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534514 true] [17592186292725 1113 #uuid "c5d5aa30-754f-54f8-9942-ed35d6ae4d72" 13194139534514 true] [17592186292725 1145 "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}+\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x,$ $a=0,$ and $b=1.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}=-\\frac{1+x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{(-\\frac{1+x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{(1+x)^{2}}{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1-{x}^{2}+1+2x+{x}^{2}}{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{2+2x}{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{2(1+x)}{(1-x)(1+x)}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{1-x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{1-x}}$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{1-x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{1-x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{2}\\sqrt{1-x}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{2}\\sqrt{1-1}-(-2\\sqrt{2}\\sqrt{1-0}) \\\\  & =0-(-2\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534514 true] [17592186292726 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292727 13194139534514 true] [17592186292726 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534514 true] [17592186292726 1041 "field-1" 13194139534514 true] [17592186292726 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292727 13194139534514 true] [17592186292726 1110 #uuid "8f415c18-c756-5943-a5cc-69a4c8c88243" 13194139534514 true] [17592186292727 1034 "2\\sqrt{2}" 13194139534514 true] [17592186292727 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534514 true] [17592186292727